# Bibliography PDF Fetcher

This repository provides a small command-line script for downloading the PDF
files referenced in a paper's bibliography. It works by extracting DOIs from
a block of citation text (or by querying Crossref when a DOI is missing) and
fetching any available PDF using the DOI link.

## Requirements

* Python 3.9 or later
* The [`requests`](https://pypi.org/project/requests/) package

Install the dependency with:

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

## Usage

Save the bibliography into a text file (for example `references.txt`) or pipe
it into the script via standard input:

```bash
python fetch_bibliography_pdfs.py --input references.txt --outdir pdfs --email your.name@example.edu
```

The script will create the specified output directory (default: `downloads`)
and store any successfully downloaded PDFs inside it. Supplying an email
address is recommended so that DOI lookups through Crossref are routed through
the polite API pool.

If your bibliography entries already contain DOIs and you want to skip Crossref
queries, pass the `--no-lookup` flag:

```bash
python fetch_bibliography_pdfs.py --no-lookup < references.txt
```

At the end of the run, a short summary highlights which references were
successfully downloaded and which ones failed (for example because a PDF was
not directly accessible via DOI).
